#{[17592186440557 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440557 #edb/ref 1069 "q-57237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440557 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440557 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{6}{7}÷2=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440557 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d44aca2-82e0-5f20-ace0-bbb17307dbfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440557 #edb/ref 1074 "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $2$ is $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{7}\\,÷\\,2=\\frac{6}{7}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{7}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{6\\times 1}{7\\times 2}=\\frac{6}{14}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{14}=\\frac{6÷2}{14÷2}=\\frac{3}{7}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440558 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440558 #edb/ref 1069 "q-211082" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440558 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440558 #edb/ref 1071 "Expressed as a fraction in its lowest terms, $\\frac{7}{8}÷10=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440558 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55d5c75e-f419-5763-b188-8a0bd660c4bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440558 #edb/ref 1074 "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $10$ is $\\frac{1}{10}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{8}\\,÷\\,10=\\frac{7}{8}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{8}\\times \\frac{1}{10}=\\frac{7\\times 1}{8\\times 10}=\\frac{7}{80}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440559 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440559 #edb/ref 1069 "q-211152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440559 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440559 #edb/ref 1071 "Expressed as a fraction in its lowest terms, $\\frac{4}{5}÷8=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440559 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "563011eb-aedf-54fc-b79c-67413e9b63b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440559 #edb/ref 1074 "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $8$ is $\\frac{1}{8}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}\\,÷\\,8=\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{4\\times 1}{5\\times 8}=\\frac{4}{40}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{40}=\\frac{4÷4}{40÷4}=\\frac{1}{10}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440560 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440560 #edb/ref 1069 "q-57092" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440560 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440560 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{3}{5}÷2=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440560 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d19cf10-06a4-535a-918f-99e1c41cec3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440560 #edb/ref 1074 "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $2$ is $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\\,÷\\,2=\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3\\times 1}{5\\times 2}=\\frac{3}{10}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440561 #edb/ref 1068 #e